module

public import Mathlib.AlgebraicGeometry.Morphisms.Etale
public import Mathlib.RingTheory.AdicCompletion.Algebra
public import Mathlib.RingTheory.FiniteType
public import Mathlib.RingTheory.Ideal.Cotangent
public import Mathlib.RingTheory.Noetherian.Defs
import Mathlib.RingTheory.AdicCompletion.LocalRing
import Mathlib.LinearAlgebra.TensorProduct.Map

/-!
# Conormal torsion of a completed retraction

Source: Stacks Project, Restricted Power Series, Tag 0AKJ,
`lemma-fully-faithful-etale-over-complement`, existence for A = C, before algebraization;
Tags 0ALQ and 0ALM (blueprint: lem-per-completed-retraction-conormal-torsion).

Maps of completions are written as R-algebra maps. Such a map is automatically linear
for the completed base: it preserves the powers of the extended ideal, and its composite
with the completed structural map is the identity, as follows modulo every power from
its R-linearity. Thus these are exactly the completed-base-algebra retractions in the node.
-/

@[expose] public section

set_option autoImplicit false

universe u

open AlgebraicGeometry

namespace AdicCompletion

/-- A power of J annihilates the conormal of the kernel of a completed retraction
from a finite type algebra etale away from V(J). The scalar in the conclusion is
explicitly the image of an element of R in the completion of S.

Source: Stacks Project, Tag 0AKJ, `lemma-fully-faithful-etale-over-complement`,
existence for A = C, using Tags 0ALQ and 0ALM
(blueprint: lem-per-completed-retraction-conormal-torsion).

Proof:
1. Write B for the completion of S and C for the completion of R. By
   `lem-per-etale-away-completed-cotangent-torsion`, B is complete with finite type
   reduction and J^c kills H^0 of its completed naive cotangent complex over R.
   Since J is finitely generated (`def-weil-pbc-noetherian-ring`),
   `lem-weil-pbc-adic-completion-mod-ideal` gives completeness of C and C/JC = R/J.
   The latter algebra is generated by the empty family over R/J.
2. The completed structural map i : C to B satisfies sigma composed with i = identity.
   Indeed R-linearity implies continuity for powers of J; modulo J^n every element
   of C comes from R, and C is separated. Therefore sigma is surjective. Both maps
   preserve powers of J. Give C its B-module structure through sigma.
3. Apply `lem-per-completed-cotangent-transitivity` to R to B to C. The zero-variable
   presentation of C over R is its identity, with kernel zero, hence zero complex.
   The zero-variable presentation of C over B is sigma, with kernel K, giving the
   complex (K/K^2 to 0). Presentation independence allows these choices. The exact
   cohomology sequence therefore injects K/K^2 into C tensor_B H^0(L completed B/R).
4. Pure tensors generate (`def-weil-pbc-module-tensor-product`), and balancing shows
   that J^c kills this tensor product because it kills H^0(L completed B/R).
   Injectivity of the connecting map gives J^c(K/K^2) = 0. K acts trivially on its
   conormal, so the B-action factors through B/K = C. Its restricted R-action is
   precisely that displayed below, since sigma composed with i is the identity. -/
theorem exists_pow_annihilates_completed_retraction_conormal
    (R : Type u) [CommRing R] [IsNoetherianRing R] (J : Ideal R)
    (S : Type u) [CommRing S] [Algebra R S]
    (hS : RingHom.FiniteType (algebraMap R S))
    (hetale : Etale (Spec.map (CommRingCat.ofHom (algebraMap R S)) ∣_
      ⟨(PrimeSpectrum.zeroLocus (J : Set R))ᶜ,
        (PrimeSpectrum.isClosed_zeroLocus (J : Set R)).isOpen_compl⟩))
    (σ : AdicCompletion (J.map (algebraMap R S)) S →ₐ[R] AdicCompletion J R) :
    ∃ c : ℕ, ∀ r ∈ J ^ c,
      ∀ x : (RingHom.ker σ.toRingHom).Cotangent,
        algebraMap R (AdicCompletion (J.map (algebraMap R S)) S) r • x = 0 := by
  sorry

end AdicCompletion
